'''Dark beasts''' are monsters that require level 90 [[Slayer]] to kill. They are found in the [[Mourner Tunnels]] under [[West Ardougne]] and in [[Iorwerth Dungeon]] in [[Prifddinas]]. Along with their [[Night beast|superior variant]], they are the only monster in the game to drop the [[dark bow]] and the [[death talisman]].

Dark beasts attack with both [[Melee]] and [[Magic]]. However, they will only use Magic as their first attack if they are attacked by the player first, or if they cannot attack the player with Melee. Dark beasts do not follow [[tolerance]] rules and are always [[aggressive]] to the player regardless of how long they have stayed in their presence. Given their highly accurate melee attacks, [[Protect from Melee]] is recommended while killing dark beasts.

In addition to level 90 Slayer, a [[combat level]] of 90 is required to have them assigned to the player as a [[Slayer task]], unless the player has spoken to a [[Slayer Master]] about the difficulty of assignments. The player also needs to have started [[Mourning's End Part II]], however no progression is required; players who do not wish to be assigned them should not continue the dialogue after completing [[Mourning's End Part I]]. 

By default, Slayer Masters aside from [[Mortimer]] will only assign 10-20 dark beasts for a Slayer task. However, the player can spend 100 [[Slayer reward point|Slayer reward points]] on ''[[Slayer Rewards|Need more darkness]]'' to extend the amount assigned to 110-135.

The fastest way to reach dark beasts is through using a [[Slayer ring]] to immediately teleport to the dark beasts in the Mourner Tunnels. This requires completion of Mourning's End Part II. Alternately, players who have completed [[Song of the Elves]] can teleport to [[Prifddinas]] to quickly reach dark beasts in the Iorwerth Dungeon. Other methods to access dark beasts are accessing the [[Death Altar]] through the [[Abyss]] to quickly reach the Mourner Tunnels or, if all else fails, entering through the [[Mourner Headquarters]] in West Ardougne.

